**Read:** Revisit the full sources and independent calculations used in all three facility investigations.

Explain how the process determines layout and barriers; how sources, paths, filters and fans set transport; and how thermal conditions, utilities, people and control change the result. Separate an intended design, an installed configuration and evidence of performance.

**Work:** Defend the three investigations together, reproduce a central result without the original calculation and revise a design conclusion after a challenged assumption. Show the consequences for the product, operators, neighboring systems and continuing service.

Continue into measurement, qualification and monitoring, deeper specialist production, operation and independent research. The facility formation establishes mechanisms and demanding studies; actual qualification requires evidence for the particular installed system and process.

